      "text": [
        " «اِسْتَخِرِ اَللَّهَ فِي آخِرِ رَكْعَةٍ مِنْ صَلاَةِ اَللَّيْلِ وَ أَنْتَ سَاجِدٌ مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ وَ مَرَّةً» قَالَ كَيْفَ أَقُولُ قَالَ «تَقُولُ أَسْتَخِيرُ اَللَّهَ بِرَحْمَتِهِ أَسْتَخِيرُ اَللَّهَ بِرَحْمَتِهِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1552 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Qasri asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about seeking divine guidance (istikhara).\nImam (as) said: \"Seek guidance from Allah (swt) in the last unit (rak'ah) of the night prayer while you are in prostration, repeating it one hundred and one times.\"\nMuhammad asked: \"How should I say it?\"\nImam (as) said: \"You should say,\nAstakheeru Allāha bi-raḥmatihi, astakheeru Allāha bi-raḥmatihi.\n'I seek guidance from Allah (swt) by His mercy, I seek guidance from Allah (swt) by His mercy.'\""
        ]
      }
    },
